I agree! Towels have dozens of potential uses that are ignored by
the current NetHack code.
For example, how about using them to dry things? Applying a towel
to metal objects or printed materials one turn after they get wet
could prevent damage.
For that matter, how about using them to clean things? I remember
my days in a dining co-op in college, scrubbing cast iron pans
with salt and vinegar because some idiot left them soaking in water
to clean them. The addition of a "potion of vinegar" or similar
substance would make a convenient, but time-consuming, way to remove
rust from armor and weapons.

